{
  "schema": "property-coercion",
  "protocol_version": "v0.1",
  "spec_section": "markdown-dialect.md §3.6.4",
  "description": "Pins the Saved Views property value-typing / coercion ruleset (markdown-dialect.md §3.6.4, MYND-271). Each case is a one-key YAML 1.2 mapping `prop: <value>`; a conformant client parses it under the YAML 1.2 CORE schema (10.2.1 — true/True/TRUE bools, base-10/hex/octal ints, NO native timestamp), takes the value of `prop`, and coerces it to exactly one Myne property type — string / number / date / list / checkbox. The date type is a Myne RFC-3339 recognizer applied to resolved string scalars (so quoting does NOT demote a date, unlike checkbox/number which a quote forces to string). Number/date normalized forms: numbers = canonical decimal of the parsed value (1.0 -> '1', 007 -> '7', 0x1A -> '26'); dates = the source string verbatim (trimmed); strings = the resolved value verbatim (no NFC). Deterministic cross-client behavior in the password-policy / note-template class (not a codec). property-index is the single type authority; sibling features consume this typing. Generated from the reference coercion (js-yaml CORE_SCHEMA + the Myne date recognizer + canonical-decimal normalization) in src/notes/propertyTyping.ts; the property-index Vitest runner asserts the live TS coercion against these vectors.",
  "cases": [
